  "schema": "xyntetik.runner.tier-smoke.v1",
  "about": "The per-release smoke of docs/model-tiers.json (scripts/tier-smoke.py): each Tier 1 file is served and asked one user turn through its own chat template (POST /v1/chat/completions, temperature 0, max_tokens n_predict, not streamed, with the request fields below), and the reply's content, as UTF-8 bytes, is byte-compared to a pin under tier-smoke/, one pin per device class and backend. The prompt asks for a fact from outside the system: a reply that does not name expect, or holds fewer than min_generated_bytes, is never pinned. The pin itself only says whether this build reproduces the one that wrote it. Each pin records the prompt and settings that produced it, how the turn ended and its completion tokens. enable_thinking false keeps a thinking family's budget for the answer; -b is fixed because the prompt batch is otherwise sized from the machine. A row may override prompt, n_predict, expect, min_generated_bytes, ctx, server_args or request.",
